md='''# Batch95 independent static QA\n\nFixed source: 5899a9f5c9e57341b42dee07ca564134bc1cbadc, candidate/small-life-batch95-concept-20261020.\n\n## Result\n\n3/4 bounded static passes: Sphenophyllum r002, Hausmannia r002, Dictyophyllum r002. Psaronius r002 fails visual acceptance. GPU and scene remain unknown for all four. No formal/user/site/release approval, no publication.\n\n## Blocking finding\n\nPsaronius has abrupt common-height transitions and black slit-like pockets between root ridges on its upper trunk. They are visible in the original hero/front/clay frames and in a fresh exact-GLB512px detail. The issue is visible root/core runout and shading interference, not a claimed open topological hole. Contact success, closed topology, uniform clay and a favorable side view do not waive this defect. Repair actual root/core geometry, preserve frozen scope/counts, then bind the new subject before fresh proof and targeted independent review. Do not conceal it with renderer/material/camera changes.\n\n## Verified\n\n-189 pins,301 available committed file blobs and555 raw-evidence files match. Fixed worktree/index remain clean. Full immutable premodel freeze and original inventory unchanged.\n-Primary text and source pixels,4 genuine concept images,32 exact final512px individual frames and4 lossless sheets personally inspected. Every sheet tile is byte-identical decoded RGB; final binding precedes real render requests.\n-Source reopened independently. Every final-source reexport is byte-identical to the shipped GLB. All4 pass project audit, Khronos0errors/0warnings and fresh Three.js GLTFLoader parses.\n-8 fresh queued rebuilds, two per asset with distinct actual PIDs, are byte- and semantic-identical. Full request/result/execution evidence retained.\n-All1657 physical interfaces pass:108 Sphenophyllum,1258 Psaronius,103 Hausmannia,186 named Dictyophyllum plus2 web/arm interfaces. Actual triangle intersections supplement surface-inside witnesses. No free centerline counted as geometry.\n-Actual authored/evaluated/exported counts, all transformed component bounds and principal dimensions measured.16 six-leaf Sphenophyllum whorls,1120 Psaronius pinnules,16 Hausmannia margin peaks,8 Dictyophyllum rays and7 actual lobes on each ray side verified.\n\n## Interpretation limits\n\nSphenophyllum whole habit/roots are hypothetical; selected fossils do not show its modeled hooks. Psaronius stays genus-level, with no species-specific crown claim from the simplex stem section. Hausmannia is an isolated half-lamina sector, not a complete organism. Dictyophyllum follows BAPb6227/6228 and the premodel correction from6 concept rays to8 final rays. Color, relief, simplified venation and nominal dimensions remain art choices. Thin organ side/top frames are naturally edge-on, not omitted.\n\n## Stage separation\n\nAll four: technical PASS, factual PASS within explicit scope, nonvisual specification PASS, runtime_parse PASS, GPU UNKNOWN, scene UNKNOWN. Visual PASS for Sphenophyllum/Hausmannia/Dictyophyllum; visual FAIL for Psaronius. No static pass grants publication.\n\nFull per-item evidence and exact hashes are in FINAL-REPORT.json. Source excerpts are local consultation only and must not be included in lean uploads. No original evidence changed or deleted.\n'''
